From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:14:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Note the Material 3 Expressive look and the material3
 1.5.0-rc01 pin in the changelog and the architecture notes, since the Android
 client's design language and its dependency pin are both decisions a future
 session should not undo by accident.

---
 AGENTS.md    | 2 +-
 CHANGELOG.md | 1 +
 CLAUDE.md    | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 160e5af..14584a7 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ Dev-only environment variables (see `capture.go`, `app/app.go`, `app/session.go`
 
 **Sign-in sources.** The saved session (`internal/auth`) comes first. If there is none, or it has expired, the app migrates the login of another client on this computer (`internal/migrate`): Baidu's own Linux client first (its Electron cookie store, read with a small pure-Go SQLite reader), then BaiduPCS-Go's active account (`internal/pcsimport`, reading `pcs_config.json`). It skips this when the user signed out on purpose (`settings.SkipImport`). The login screen also offers it as a link. Every sign-in is saved at once, and saved again when `Client.Credentials` changes (the uid found, cookies the netdisk rotated; `Client.OnChange`) and on quit.
 
-**Android client (`android/`).** A second product in the same repository: a Kotlin + Jetpack Compose Material 3 app built with Gradle (AGP 9.4.1, Kotlin 2.4.20, Compose BOM 2026.09.00, compileSdk 37, minSdk 26), entirely separate from `go build`. It shares no code with the desktop app but speaks the same netdisk protocol (the pan.baidu.com web endpoints plus `/api/precreate` → `pcs/superfile2` parts → `/api/create`), the same backup layout and the same `.gpg` format, so the two halves back up into one netdisk folder. `:core` (pure JVM, `com.pengstem.baidunetgo.core`) holds `net/BaiduApi` (client, chunked upload, QR sign-in), `crypto/Pgp` (BouncyCastle bcpg; BouncyCastle's v5 session-key quirk had to be turned off for gpg/Go compatibility) and `backup/` (the incremental engine over a `Netdisk` interface and a `BackupSource`, so MediaStore albums and SAF trees are just sources); `:app` (`com.pengstem.baidunetgo`) holds the Compose screens, MediaStore album scanning, the SAF folder picker, Keystore-encrypted storage, WorkManager periodic workers and the foreground backup service. `android/docs/CORE-API.md` is the contract between them. Tests: `./gradlew :core:test` runs the client against `cmd/fakepand` (the same `internal/fakepan`, started as a process and its `url=…` line read from stdout; `FAKEPAN_URL` reuses one) and OpenPGP against the real `gpg` in both directions, and `:app:testDebugUnitTest` holds codec/path tests plus Robolectric renders written to `android/screenshots/` (there is no emulator here: no `/dev/kvm`). Builds need `ANDROID_HOME`, `JAVA_HOME` (JDK 21) and a writable `GRADLE_USER_HOME`; `android/keystore/dev.jks` is a public dev-only keystore for `assembleDebug`. `docs/ANDROID.md` is the hand-over (build, CI notes, update-channel idea).
+**Android client (`android/`).** A second product in the same repository: a Kotlin + Jetpack Compose Material 3 app built with Gradle (AGP 9.4.1, Kotlin 2.4.20, Compose BOM 2026.09.00 with Material 3 1.5.0-rc01 pinned for its public Material 3 Expressive API, compileSdk 37, minSdk 26), entirely separate from `go build`. It shares no code with the desktop app but speaks the same netdisk protocol (the pan.baidu.com web endpoints plus `/api/precreate` → `pcs/superfile2` parts → `/api/create`), the same backup layout and the same `.gpg` format, so the two halves back up into one netdisk folder. `:core` (pure JVM, `com.pengstem.baidunetgo.core`) holds `net/BaiduApi` (client, chunked upload, QR sign-in), `crypto/Pgp` (BouncyCastle bcpg; BouncyCastle's v5 session-key quirk had to be turned off for gpg/Go compatibility) and `backup/` (the incremental engine over a `Netdisk` interface and a `BackupSource`, so MediaStore albums and SAF trees are just sources); `:app` (`com.pengstem.baidunetgo`) holds the Compose screens, MediaStore album scanning, the SAF folder picker, Keystore-encrypted storage, WorkManager periodic workers and the foreground backup service. The look is Material 3 Expressive (`MaterialExpressiveTheme` + `MotionScheme.expressive()`, rounded `surfaceBright` cards, expressive switches and segmented rows, a floating tonal navigation bar), following the Material mode of KernelSU rather than its Miuix or liquid-glass variants. `android/docs/CORE-API.md` is the contract between them. Tests: `./gradlew :core:test` runs the client against `cmd/fakepand` (the same `internal/fakepan`, started as a process and its `url=…` line read from stdout; `FAKEPAN_URL` reuses one) and OpenPGP against the real `gpg` in both directions, and `:app:testDebugUnitTest` holds codec/path tests plus Robolectric renders written to `android/screenshots/` (there is no emulator here: no `/dev/kvm`). Builds need `ANDROID_HOME`, `JAVA_HOME` (JDK 21) and a writable `GRADLE_USER_HOME`; `android/keystore/dev.jks` is a public dev-only keystore for `assembleDebug`. `docs/ANDROID.md` is the hand-over (build, CI notes, update-channel idea).
 
 **One keyring key for every build.** `mygo.Secrets` names its service after the build (`<identifier>.dev` under `mygo dev`, the app name under `go run`, the identifier when packaged), so `OpenStore` pins the key to `com.pengstem.baidunetgo`. `auth.Store.Older` lists the old services: `Load` tries their keys and saves the session again under the pinned one.
 
diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index d0db857..f80a7aa 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 
 ### 改进
 
+- Android 端的界面改为 **Material 3 Expressive**：主题换成 `MaterialExpressiveTheme` 并启用 `MotionScheme.expressive()` 的弹簧动效，卡片改为 `surfaceBright` 圆角色调卡（圆角 20 dp）、开关带对勾指示、并发 / 间隔 / 主题 / 全选这类选择改用胶囊分段控件，底部导航变成浮起的色调胶囊（选中项是药丸形指示），对话框与输入框用大圆角；参考 KernelSU 的 Material 实现（它的 Miuix 与液态玻璃组件没有采用）。为使用公开的 Expressive API，`material3` 在版本目录里显式钉到 `1.5.0-rc01`（BOM 里的 1.4.0 仍把该 API 标为 internal）。视觉调整见 `android/screenshots/`（Robolectric 无头渲染）。
 - 大文件夹的列表与上传中的文件夹更省：每帧不再为全部文件建行位置表（只有文件进出、行高不同时才建）、不再每帧重新格式化每行的字节数 / 日期 / 类型（按 fs_id 缓存，读目录或跨天时更新）、行位置与行矩形等 map 改为跨帧复用、「选择栏」与「是否只选了一项」不再为计数而复制整个选择、右键菜单的闭包改为持有文件指针；上传中的临时行与目录列表的比对从「每个上传 × 全部文件」改成按名字集合一次比对。2000 个文件的列表一帧的分配从 105 KB 降到 23 KB（GC 次数约降为原来的四分之一），50 个上传同时涌入时一帧从 822 µs 降到 516 µs；传输页在 200 个任务时不再每帧重新切分任务列表、重新格式化每行详情、重新统计工具栏（按任务变更计数缓存进行中 / 已完成两份列表与计数，每帧分配从 145 KB 降到 14.5 KB），文件进出时行的位置表改用保留的 `[]float32`（一次 −83%、0 分配），快捷键处理也不再在每帧开头复制一遍整个选择。测量方法、前后对比与剩下的热点见 [docs/PERFORMANCE.md](docs/PERFORMANCE.md)。
 - 框选后用左键单击列表或网格的空白处取消选择，与 Esc 及选择栏的「取消选择」一致；按住 ⌘ 单击空白保留选择（追加语义），单击行 / 瓦片仍照常改选，框选松开本身不会误清。
 - 新增「拖动即移动」：在列表或网格中按住文件 / 文件夹拖动并放到另一个文件夹行、文件夹瓦片或面包屑上即可移动过去，拖动时跟随指针显示半透明卡片（多项显示「N 项」），可投放的目标会高亮；拖到空白处或窗口外取消，同名交给冲突对话框，拖进自身或其子目录会被拒绝。左键拖动项目不再多选。
